on CUDA/HIP the untuned plan seeds a contraction: true
where the untuned compile splits (CUDA and HIP), the plan splits a reduction: true
off CUDA/HIP the untuned compile is the plain default: true
off CUDA/HIP the search derives no seeded plan: true
the search's first candidate is the seeded untuned plan: true
every attempt of the seeded plan compiled and reached a timing window: true
its timed code is the untuned compile's, segment for segment: true
the search went on to time later candidates, every one of them refused: true
the search crowned the seeded plan, its reading the report's seeded_ms and best_ms: true
the crowned gradients are bitwise the untuned compile's: true
the control: the plain default pipeline's bias gradient differs in some cell: true
in the refused-seed search too, every seeded attempt compiled and was timed: true
a refused seeded window is retried once, before the singles inside it: true
the retried seeded plan is crowned and reported as seeded_ms: true
a search that times nothing returns the untuned compile's gradients, bitwise: true
a search-less tune with no cache ships the untuned compile's gradients, bitwise: true
a search-less tune whose cache misses ships the untuned compile's gradients, bitwise: true
under seed A the search is abandoned after its first timed candidates: true
control: seed A again replays that abandonment without timing anything: true
under seed B the same trajectory searches rather than replay seed A's abandonment: true
under seed A the search completes and records its steps: true
control: seed A again replays the crown with its steps: true
under seed B the crown replays without seed A's steps: true
not every store of the two-seed sequences was refused: true
